WEBVTT

00:37.890 --> 00:38.690
Stop smoking.

00:38.930 --> 00:40.660
Its smell affects my judgment.

00:48.210 --> 00:49.610
I'll quit smoking, okay?

01:25.650 --> 01:26.900
Two days are

01:27.539 --> 01:28.430
enough.

01:28.570 --> 01:35.590
[Countdown: 48 Hours]

01:30.780 --> 01:31.430
Shrimpie,

01:33.650 --> 01:34.780
I'll bring you back.

01:37.430 --> 01:38.289
Heavenly Hand.

01:38.840 --> 01:39.840
Come on, pay up.

01:39.930 --> 01:42.860
How did you win again?
I haven't even sorted my tiles.

01:45.789 --> 01:47.090
What can we find out from this?

01:47.090 --> 01:48.470
Do you have any extra cash?

01:48.470 --> 01:49.470
Give me some more.

01:50.920 --> 01:52.380
I'll wait for you outside.

01:56.430 --> 01:57.340
I haven't sorted my tiles yet.

01:57.340 --> 01:57.789
Here.

01:58.590 --> 01:59.180
Guys,

02:00.510 --> 02:02.370
has anything really odd happened

02:02.380 --> 02:03.440
on the ship lately?

02:03.500 --> 02:04.430
Tell me about it.

02:05.620 --> 02:06.400
Around here,

02:06.540 --> 02:08.250
weird things happen every day.

02:08.250 --> 02:09.979
Which one are you asking about?

02:10.080 --> 02:11.030
Things like

02:11.860 --> 02:13.720
someone eating something harmful,

02:13.720 --> 02:15.850
or something suddenly going missing.

02:15.860 --> 02:16.590
Those all count.

02:16.590 --> 02:18.210
I actually do have a story.

02:19.040 --> 02:20.360
But it's not about a thing—

02:20.360 --> 02:21.970
it's about a person. Does that count?

02:21.970 --> 02:22.550
Sure, it counts.

02:22.550 --> 02:23.130
This guy is

02:23.130 --> 02:24.180
called Song Cai.

02:24.620 --> 02:25.620
He's also a sailor.

02:25.620 --> 02:26.900
A week ago,

02:27.030 --> 02:30.130
when the ship just arrived at Balai port,

02:30.360 --> 02:31.490
he was still around.

02:31.730 --> 02:33.520
But when it was time to set sail again,

02:33.520 --> 02:35.180
he suddenly disappeared without a trace.

02:35.180 --> 02:36.340
Did he jump into the sea?

02:36.340 --> 02:36.870
Nope.

02:37.540 --> 02:38.920
Song Cai's disappearance

02:38.920 --> 02:40.450
was very peculiar.

02:41.829 --> 02:44.050
When cleaning his room,

02:44.510 --> 02:46.570
someone found a box under his bed.

02:47.000 --> 02:49.360
Inside it were bottles full of flies.

02:49.380 --> 02:49.960
Flies?

02:49.980 --> 02:50.510
Exactly.

02:50.520 --> 02:52.120
Like, whole bottles full of live flies.

02:52.120 --> 02:52.880
Rumor has it

02:52.940 --> 02:55.590
that Song Cai caught them himself
on the ship before he disappeared.

02:55.590 --> 02:57.750
I heard from the guys whom he lived with

02:59.000 --> 03:01.840
that ever since Song Cai arrived in Balai,

03:01.860 --> 03:03.660
he had been acting really weird.

03:03.970 --> 03:05.080
He would often

03:05.310 --> 03:07.420
sneak out in the middle of the night,

03:07.930 --> 03:09.860
probably just to catch flies.

03:25.150 --> 03:27.010
Is the Song Cai you just mentioned

03:27.490 --> 03:28.400
Chinese?

03:29.680 --> 03:30.090
Yes.

03:30.090 --> 03:30.690
Yep.

03:31.329 --> 03:32.440
When did he go missing?

03:32.440 --> 03:33.480
Just a couple of days ago,

03:33.480 --> 03:34.660
around early July.

03:35.560 --> 03:36.530
These 3 villages were

03:36.530 --> 03:38.620
where the issue of Twilight Grass
first broke out at the same time.

03:36.600 --> 03:39.220
[Xucheng] [Got poisoned on the ship—
the Nan'an] [Xiacheng]

03:39.290 --> 03:40.490
And in all 3 villages,

03:40.760 --> 03:41.910
the first poisoned individuals

03:41.910 --> 03:43.500
all had boarded the Nan'an

03:43.400 --> 03:45.900
[When were they poisoned?]
[The first poisoned individuals] [July 2]

03:43.930 --> 03:46.590
from Xiacheng to Balai
in the first week of July.

03:47.740 --> 03:49.260
Do you know which room he stayed in?

03:49.260 --> 03:49.890
I know.

03:52.850 --> 03:53.480
Well...

03:55.030 --> 03:56.260
Take me there, will you?

03:56.260 --> 03:58.570
[Song Cai's Dormitory]

04:00.370 --> 04:01.900
Here we are. It's this room.

04:06.580 --> 04:07.440
This is his bed.

04:11.790 --> 04:15.190
Was Song Cai using flies
to spread the Twilight Grass Poison?

04:18.640 --> 04:19.769
Where are the flies?

04:20.730 --> 04:21.630
We threw them away

04:21.630 --> 04:22.490
a long time ago.

04:27.120 --> 04:27.980
Well,

04:28.190 --> 04:29.010
take your time looking.

04:29.010 --> 04:30.070
I'll take my leave.

04:32.360 --> 04:33.190
Do you know

04:33.860 --> 04:36.190
that a first-class ticket on the Nan'an

04:36.890 --> 04:39.750
costs as much
as an ordinary person earns in 3 years?

04:39.790 --> 04:41.340
What do you do, Mr. Zhang,

04:41.620 --> 04:44.150
to be able to afford
such an expensive ticket?

04:44.690 --> 04:46.020
I'm just a spendthrift.

04:48.040 --> 04:49.080
My uncle is rich.

04:51.540 --> 04:53.220
Now it's my turn to ask you a question.

04:53.220 --> 04:55.150
Flies can spread bacteria, right?

04:55.280 --> 04:55.790
Yes.

04:56.190 --> 04:58.440
Can flies be controlled by humans, then?

04:58.440 --> 04:59.159
For example,

04:59.159 --> 05:02.340
can someone intentionally
place them in a specific area

05:02.600 --> 05:04.310
to spread something along a certain route?

05:04.310 --> 05:04.770
No.

05:05.160 --> 05:05.750
Why?

05:08.190 --> 05:10.990
I've never seen anyone who can tame flies.

05:11.990 --> 05:13.660
A fly's flight path

05:13.680 --> 05:16.010
cannot be predicted precisely.

05:16.190 --> 05:18.920
If bacteria had been transmitted
through flies,

05:18.920 --> 05:20.760
the outbreak would have spread
on a massive

05:20.760 --> 05:22.290
and uncontrollable scale.

05:22.390 --> 05:26.160
There's no way it would be limited
to just some small areas.

05:28.440 --> 05:29.840
So you have common sense.

05:33.600 --> 05:36.310
Could it be
that Song Cai is really not the culprit?

05:36.310 --> 05:37.870
The flies couldn't be trained

05:37.870 --> 05:40.690
to specifically spread the poison
to 3 villages, right?

05:40.690 --> 05:42.550
Now it's my turn to ask questions.

05:43.480 --> 05:44.520
Do the flies

05:44.710 --> 05:47.840
have anything to do
with the case you are investigating?

05:49.220 --> 05:51.900
[N P]

05:50.300 --> 05:52.180
N-P?

05:58.880 --> 06:01.150
[N P]

06:08.100 --> 06:09.190
[N P]

06:20.980 --> 06:22.180
You know Latin?

06:25.000 --> 06:27.880
This is a local, common phrase in Balai.

06:27.900 --> 06:29.130
It originally referred

06:29.130 --> 06:31.600
to a potion that the Queen of Egypt
gave to Helen.

06:31.600 --> 06:33.800
This word has another meaning in Balai.

06:34.150 --> 06:35.350
It can refer to a plant

06:36.010 --> 06:37.540
known as the pitcher plant.

06:39.920 --> 06:42.320
But what does the pitcher plant represent?

06:42.690 --> 06:46.420
And what is the connection
between the flies and the pitcher plant?

06:48.450 --> 06:48.980
Bro,

06:50.430 --> 06:52.230
you told me that you could help me

06:54.000 --> 06:56.060
with anything these two days, right?

07:23.950 --> 07:24.630
Steven,

07:24.920 --> 07:25.720
jobs are done.

07:39.250 --> 07:40.490
It's the end of the day.

07:40.490 --> 07:41.360
Mr. Zhang,

07:41.800 --> 07:44.180
is there any progress
on catching the culprit?

07:44.180 --> 07:46.180
Actually, this is all my intuition.

07:46.330 --> 07:47.450
I just took a bit of a detour,

07:47.450 --> 07:48.240
my friend.

07:48.860 --> 07:49.740
But you have to believe me,

07:49.740 --> 07:51.470
as my intuition is never wrong.

07:52.230 --> 07:52.950
So

07:53.190 --> 07:55.010
you've been fooling me for half a day?

07:55.010 --> 07:55.930
Why so impatient?

07:55.930 --> 07:57.530
We still have a day and a half.

07:59.340 --> 08:00.760
Miss Dong is

08:01.930 --> 08:04.330
a woman worth ingratiating yourself with.

08:05.080 --> 08:06.720
Work with me and do your best.

08:07.120 --> 08:08.180
This is your chance

08:08.750 --> 08:10.210
to make a good impression.

08:10.770 --> 08:12.980
Mr. Zhang, half a day has already passed.

08:12.980 --> 08:15.270
We will continue at 7:00 a.m. tomorrow.

08:18.060 --> 08:24.900
[Countdown: 36 Hours]

08:42.750 --> 08:43.549
The red stains

08:44.460 --> 08:45.390
are human blood.

08:46.200 --> 08:47.240
I knew I'd find something.

08:46.410 --> 08:54.870
[Medical Reserve Room]

08:49.170 --> 08:50.430
Medical reserve room?

09:24.520 --> 09:26.210
The flies must have flown in

09:26.240 --> 09:27.770
through the passage ahead.

09:45.900 --> 09:48.110
[The bottom hold of the Nan'an]

10:10.840 --> 10:12.570
There was a fierce battle here.

11:13.870 --> 11:15.930
Why does this place look so familiar?

11:28.220 --> 11:30.550
Why is there so much mud
in the bottom hold?

12:09.410 --> 12:11.980
I want to see what the hell you're up to.

13:02.100 --> 13:06.030
Why is the ancestral shrine of Evil God
in the bottom hold of the Nan'an?

13:17.170 --> 13:19.030
Now this is getting interesting.

14:47.600 --> 14:54.130
[Archives: The Nanyang Mystery]

14:54.540 --> 14:57.190
[Episode 5]

15:26.980 --> 15:29.450
How could this be inside the ship?

15:32.170 --> 15:34.150
Holy shit!

15:39.630 --> 15:40.360
You're here.

15:44.630 --> 15:45.600
I told you that

15:46.170 --> 15:48.430
we could find clues following the flies.

15:48.790 --> 15:49.720
I was right, huh?

15:50.750 --> 15:51.280
Let's go.

16:06.170 --> 16:07.100
Where are we?

16:08.440 --> 16:09.370
What's going on?

16:12.740 --> 16:14.540
I've been at sea longer than you.

16:15.390 --> 16:17.090
This must be the way you Easterners

16:17.090 --> 16:18.530
smuggle antiques.

16:18.650 --> 16:21.380
You Easterners have
plenty of methods like this.

16:23.460 --> 16:24.660
I think you're right.

16:28.200 --> 16:28.620
Why

16:28.640 --> 16:29.920
are you sticking to me?

16:29.990 --> 16:31.030
To protect you.

16:31.510 --> 16:32.170
Protect me?

16:32.960 --> 16:35.420
Is there something here
that will attack us?

16:35.740 --> 16:36.840
Didn't you just say

16:38.010 --> 16:38.650
this might be

16:38.650 --> 16:40.380
a place for antique smuggling?

16:41.050 --> 16:42.050
Then someone might

16:42.050 --> 16:43.110
come and attack us.

16:45.010 --> 16:46.210
Wouldn't that be you?

17:00.290 --> 17:01.150
Look over there.

17:01.150 --> 17:01.720
Where?

17:03.080 --> 17:03.940
There's a hole.

17:05.440 --> 17:07.380
Do you see that mark on this hole?

17:08.380 --> 17:10.310
We need to put something inside it,

17:10.819 --> 17:12.260
and then a stone door will open,

17:12.260 --> 17:13.390
revealing a passage

17:15.060 --> 17:17.390
that leads to the place we're looking for.

17:17.500 --> 17:19.420
How do you know a door will open?

17:19.650 --> 17:20.780
Just a random guess.

17:23.569 --> 17:25.300
Then what should we put in here?

17:27.880 --> 17:29.740
What are you holding in your hand?

17:39.870 --> 17:41.070
It's a nice day today.

17:42.840 --> 17:43.770
Get ready later.

17:44.550 --> 17:46.210
This is the crew's god statue.

17:46.480 --> 17:48.090
You took it, and they will riot!

17:48.090 --> 17:49.350
You're exaggerating.

17:49.670 --> 17:50.590
Hear me out.

17:50.610 --> 17:52.300
It's my old acquaintance.

17:52.500 --> 17:54.180
We're very familiar with each other.
Nothing will happen.

17:54.180 --> 17:55.380
Come on, give it to me.

17:55.530 --> 17:58.230
I am now arresting you for stealing stuff

17:58.270 --> 17:59.070
from the ship!

17:59.330 --> 18:01.500
We are only one step away
from solving the case.

18:01.500 --> 18:02.830
The truth is behind this thing.

18:02.830 --> 18:03.930
Why should I believe you?

18:03.930 --> 18:05.230
I will absolutely never trust you again!

18:05.230 --> 18:06.530
Fine! If you don't believe me,

18:06.530 --> 18:07.530
just shoot me now!

18:07.530 --> 18:08.460
You said it yourself!

18:08.460 --> 18:10.260
I said it! Come on! Draw your gun!

18:16.230 --> 18:17.490
There really is a door.

18:18.400 --> 18:19.750
You've definitely been here.

18:19.750 --> 18:20.570
This is not a door.

18:20.570 --> 18:22.100
I haven't been here before!

18:34.000 --> 18:35.860
If it's not a door, then what is it?

18:37.010 --> 18:38.270
This is not important.

18:39.050 --> 18:40.780
What's inside is what matters.

18:41.740 --> 18:43.200
Let's go in and take a look.

19:10.900 --> 19:12.680
How did you know this god statue

19:13.170 --> 19:14.430
could open this door?

19:21.280 --> 19:22.810
Don't play any more tricks.

19:24.150 --> 19:25.750
Let me show you a magic trick.

19:50.960 --> 19:53.160
Black magic. It's all your black magic!

19:55.050 --> 19:56.310
It's Nanyang black magic.

19:56.310 --> 19:57.240
But don't worry.

19:57.770 --> 20:00.170
I'm very good
at handling things like this.

20:00.460 --> 20:02.860
Otherwise, how could I be
a patrolman here?

20:31.220 --> 20:32.860
What about that big Evil God?

20:49.380 --> 20:51.610
I'm Zhang Siye
from the Xiacheng Headquarters

20:51.610 --> 20:53.550
of the Southern Archives.

20:55.960 --> 20:57.350
So it's you.

20:58.900 --> 21:00.350
You didn't die back then

21:00.380 --> 21:01.800
until you crawled here.

21:02.070 --> 21:02.810
Now I know

21:02.810 --> 21:05.540
why Zhang Ruipu could
make it out alive back then.

21:06.270 --> 21:08.130
So he escaped through this hole.

21:09.190 --> 21:10.580
The answer lies in this hole.

21:10.580 --> 21:11.780
Let's go in and check.

21:11.830 --> 21:14.030
What will happen if we go into this hole?

21:14.040 --> 21:15.120
Keep this for me.

21:15.240 --> 21:15.740
No, no.

21:45.420 --> 21:47.220
When was the last time you cried?

21:48.510 --> 21:50.350
I haven't cried once since I was 3.

21:50.350 --> 21:51.290
I'm sure that

21:51.740 --> 21:54.070
the next time you cry
will be in 30 minutes.

21:54.260 --> 21:55.020
Why?

21:55.590 --> 21:57.520
What comes next will be really terrifying.

21:57.520 --> 21:58.090
Let's go

21:59.230 --> 22:01.030
investigate the case together.

22:08.560 --> 22:10.380
Oh, Jesus!

22:30.750 --> 22:31.460
I'm sorry.

22:32.110 --> 22:32.550
I...

22:33.660 --> 22:34.880
feel suffocated.

22:35.070 --> 22:37.010
So I'm chewing some tobacco.

22:40.240 --> 22:41.270
Why didn't you share

22:41.270 --> 22:42.600
such good stuff with me?

22:46.090 --> 22:46.890
Stop smoking.

22:47.460 --> 22:49.190
Its smell affects my judgment.

22:53.160 --> 22:54.690
I'll keep it for you for now.

23:12.590 --> 23:13.550
Someone's there.

23:13.550 --> 23:14.960
Nanyang Fast Gun, get ready.

23:14.960 --> 23:16.020
Get ready for what?

23:32.980 --> 23:33.570
Well...

23:34.100 --> 23:35.190
Isn't this a mirror?

23:35.190 --> 23:36.190
It's not a mirror.

23:36.970 --> 23:37.780
I'm not in it.

23:38.250 --> 23:39.440
Are you a vampire?

23:43.900 --> 23:44.840
Are you an idiot?

23:50.090 --> 23:52.110
I see it clearly. This is a mirror.

23:52.130 --> 23:53.450
It's a dead end.

23:53.670 --> 23:54.950
We should go back.

23:56.230 --> 23:57.030
Wait a minute!

23:58.220 --> 23:58.820
What's up?

23:59.830 --> 24:00.290
Look.

24:05.010 --> 24:05.860
Let go of me.

24:06.040 --> 24:07.040
This is a dead end.

24:07.530 --> 24:09.390
We should either find another way

24:09.520 --> 24:10.350
or head back.

24:10.530 --> 24:12.790
I told you, this is a place for smuggling.

24:15.390 --> 24:16.830
We need to hurry back.

24:16.830 --> 24:17.610
I want to go back!

24:17.610 --> 24:19.070
Come back! Come back here!

24:28.400 --> 24:30.260
Damn it, I have had enough.

24:30.290 --> 24:32.430
I want to go back home,

24:32.450 --> 24:35.100
take a hot bath, and lie in a warm bed.

24:35.270 --> 24:35.900
Fast Gun!

24:35.940 --> 24:37.270
And end this nightmare.

24:37.380 --> 24:38.150
Steven.

24:39.910 --> 24:40.660
Fast Gun.

24:41.610 --> 24:42.460
Fast Gun.

24:43.610 --> 24:44.370
Fast Gun!

24:49.440 --> 24:50.240
Fast Gun.

24:51.200 --> 24:51.870
I am real.

24:52.350 --> 24:53.090
I am real.

24:59.830 --> 25:01.490
I didn't believe him just now.

25:02.860 --> 25:04.320
You have to believe me now.

25:07.140 --> 25:08.070
You can't leave!

25:13.200 --> 25:14.550
You scared me!

25:14.570 --> 25:15.690
How dare you hit me?

25:20.610 --> 25:22.200
What should we do now?

25:23.460 --> 25:25.190
Let me think. Give me some time.

25:26.550 --> 25:28.680
What would Shrimpie do if he were here?

25:30.870 --> 25:33.420
First of all,
this thing is definitely not real.

25:33.420 --> 25:35.670
Secondly, it didn't take
the initiative to attack us.

25:35.670 --> 25:37.530
Then there's only one option now.

25:38.050 --> 25:38.900
That is to join them.

25:38.900 --> 25:40.360
What kind of logic is that?

25:47.470 --> 25:49.470
Shh.

26:26.220 --> 26:28.820
Seems like all of this is
just a hallucination.

26:29.070 --> 26:29.800
Listen to me.

26:30.640 --> 26:32.060
We can ignore them now.

26:32.540 --> 26:33.870
Just go straight ahead.

26:34.200 --> 26:35.660
We'll definitely be fine.

26:39.680 --> 26:40.900
Mom!

26:41.290 --> 26:41.920
Calm down.

26:54.330 --> 26:55.060
Keep it down.

27:10.930 --> 27:12.860
Bro, you're messing with me again.

27:56.350 --> 27:57.250
Fast Gun,

27:58.400 --> 27:59.310
we won.

28:00.480 --> 28:01.740
Now we can keep...

28:14.420 --> 28:15.400
I get it now.

28:16.110 --> 28:17.710
This is all a hallucination.

28:19.000 --> 28:21.660
So I've been in a hallucination
this whole time.

28:21.900 --> 28:24.410
That foreigner never followed me.

28:25.180 --> 28:26.640
It's been just me all along.

28:26.640 --> 28:27.750
Right, that's it.

28:27.770 --> 28:28.260
Help!

28:29.460 --> 28:30.310
Help!

28:30.810 --> 28:31.940
Salty Zhang!

28:32.750 --> 28:33.640
I'm here!

28:35.930 --> 28:37.070
Why are you down there?

28:37.070 --> 28:38.200
There's a hole here.

28:38.410 --> 28:39.670
I accidentally fell in.

28:39.670 --> 28:40.770
Help me!

28:52.240 --> 28:54.240
Alright, don't cry.

28:55.010 --> 28:57.070
Didn't I tell you in advance earlier?

28:58.750 --> 29:01.280
This will be the last time you cry
in your life.

29:01.820 --> 29:02.600
Right?

29:03.330 --> 29:04.250
But it's fine.

29:05.510 --> 29:06.180
We now

29:06.920 --> 29:08.450
have a hostage in our hands.

29:08.790 --> 29:10.120
Keep this hostage safe.

29:12.240 --> 29:13.480
If anything happens,

29:13.500 --> 29:14.990
just break its head.

29:15.200 --> 29:16.400
It's very effective.

29:21.390 --> 29:21.990
Have some.

29:39.350 --> 29:40.880
Keep what just happened

29:41.530 --> 29:43.660
only between us.

29:43.660 --> 29:44.320
Otherwise,

29:44.750 --> 29:47.410
I'll make sure
you won't even survive for 2 days.

29:50.250 --> 29:50.830
Okay,

29:52.000 --> 29:52.920
I got it.

29:53.810 --> 29:54.830
But how did you fall

29:54.830 --> 29:55.960
into this crevice?

29:56.340 --> 29:58.400
Weren't you right behind me just now?

29:58.960 --> 29:59.550
I...

29:59.880 --> 30:00.660
I don't know.

30:01.810 --> 30:03.540
Just now, when I turned around,

30:03.660 --> 30:04.660
I happened to make

30:04.740 --> 30:06.870
eye contact with that thing behind me.

30:07.070 --> 30:08.270
My vision went black,

30:08.640 --> 30:09.500
and I fell down.

30:10.230 --> 30:11.590
Anyway, based on my observation,

30:11.590 --> 30:13.720
there don't seem to be any robbers here.

30:13.720 --> 30:15.940
We'd better hurry and find a way out.

30:16.020 --> 30:18.680
Yeah, what could this have to do
with the robber?

30:20.590 --> 30:22.190
But it's quite interesting.

30:22.440 --> 30:23.720
I followed the clues about Song Cai

30:23.720 --> 30:24.750
and somehow ended up finding

30:24.750 --> 30:26.610
this ancestral shrine of Evil God.

30:26.610 --> 30:27.880
And this ancestral shrine of Evil God

30:27.880 --> 30:29.220
was the one I...

30:34.200 --> 30:35.110
Do you think

30:35.590 --> 30:38.590
this is a coincidence,
or someone set it up on purpose?

30:38.740 --> 30:39.380
I...

30:42.390 --> 30:44.190
Catching the robber is your job.

30:44.940 --> 30:46.140
Once the 2 days are up,

30:46.600 --> 30:47.290
I will...

30:53.830 --> 30:55.990
I also smell this corpse stench.

30:57.010 --> 30:57.720
This way.

31:13.920 --> 31:15.050
Give me the hostage.

31:21.440 --> 31:22.090
Why?

31:22.660 --> 31:23.350
For safety.

31:24.290 --> 31:25.350
